# Build synthetic and opt-in integration evidence

## Goal

Prove behavior deterministically without making a real mailbox part of ordinary
development or CI.

## Required work

- Build synthetic IMAP and SMTP fixtures with deterministic time and IDs.
- Cover disconnects, timeouts, malformed MIME, partial batches, and ambiguity.
- Create a separately gated live-account suite.
- Prevent live tests from running through default Cargo commands.
- Scan fixtures and logs for credential-shaped material.

## Acceptance criteria

- Default tests need no network or credentials.
- Live tests require an explicit feature and opt-in environment signal.
- Failure artifacts contain no message bodies or secrets.
- Tests cover every declared safety class.

## Evidence

- Deterministic integration suite
- Live-test isolation regression
- Secret-scan result
